WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.147
The notebook example follows a simple sequence.

00:00:04.147 --> 00:00:07.077
First, Spark reads a file into a data frame.

00:00:07.077 --> 00:00:11.677
Second, that data frame is registered as a temporary view.

00:00:11.677 --> 00:00:16.112
Third, Spark S Q L queries the temporary view.

00:00:16.112 --> 00:00:19.752
Do not focus on memorizing every function call.

00:00:19.752 --> 00:00:24.797
Focus on the flow: file, data frame, temporary view, then S Q L.

00:00:24.797 --> 00:00:33.042
This code requires a real Spark environment, so it is not intended to run inside the small browser S Q L practice engine

00:00:33.042 --> 00:00:35.324
used in the course.
